         "type":"string",
         "value":"The paper discusses the use of satellite microwave and infrared radiometric imagery for monitoring volcanic plumes and ash clouds. Figures 2 and 3 show VIIRS data at 05:08 and 19:08 UTC, with brightness temperatures and ash cloud masks. Figures 4 and 5 show ATMS data at the same times, with microwave brightness temperatures. Figure 6 shows the combination of MW and TIR signatures, and Figures 7 and 8 show estimates of tephra mass loading and mass flow rate."
